CDEadmin hard-fork notice and upstream attribution
==================================================

CDEadmin is an independent hard fork of pgAdmin 4, based on pgAdmin 4 9.17.
CDEadmin is a separate multi-engine, multi-model database administration product and is not pgAdmin 4. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by the pgAdmin Development Team.

The upstream pgAdmin 4 code is Copyright (C) 2013 - 2026, The pgAdmin Development Team and is distributed under the PostgreSQL Licence. CDEadmin
continues to be distributed under the PostgreSQL Licence. The repository
LICENSE file, upstream copyright headers, source history, and applicable
third-party notices are retained and must be included in derived
distributions.

CDEadmin modifications are copyright their respective contributors.

Major divergences from the upstream project include a provider-driven engine
architecture, native ScratchBird support, management of independent reference
engines, relational and non-relational administration, multi-model query
workspaces, analytic semantic models and cubes, and distributed-system
control-plane administration. ScratchBird emulation endpoints are deliberately
treated like the corresponding native engine rather than as a special product
mode.

The active product name and visual identity are CDEadmin. Legacy identifiers
such as the Python package `pgadmin`, JavaScript object `pgAdmin`, environment
prefix `PGADMIN_`, and launcher `pgAdmin4.py` are retained only where changing
them would break upstream API, configuration, migration, extension, or build
compatibility. They do not identify the product shown to users. New
CDEadmin-owned code must use CDEadmin names.

The pgAdmin name and artwork are not CDEadmin product assets. PostgreSQL and
the names of supported database engines are used only to identify supported
technologies and their engine-specific administration surfaces. Their owners
retain all rights in their names and marks.

CDEadmin signing identities and update channels are independent and remain
unassigned. A CDEadmin release is not yet approved until product, legal,
security, and release-engineering controls are completed.
